  era: "Section 11 \xB7 Post-Gupta Period \xB7 c. 550 \u2013 1000 CE"
  title: Pushyabhutis
  text: The Pushyabhuti, or Vardhana, dynasty began at Thanesar in Haryana. Prabhakaravardhana resisted the Hunas, and his sons Rajyavardhana and Harshavardhana followed him. Harsha moved the capital to Kannauj, which became the great prize of north Indian politics.
